 "title": "Electricity and Magnetism (2nd edition)",
 "byline": "B. I. Bleaney and B. Bleaney · Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1965",
 "note": "PDF page = printed page + 13. This is a scanned copy with an OCR text layer; its own contents page for chapters 1–4 is missing, so those sections were recovered from the body text. Summaries and terms are per chapter; each section is listed with its PDF page range. Problems and appendices are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A classic Oxford undergraduate and early-graduate text covering electricity and magnetism from first principles to the physics of materials, in rationalized m.k.s. units. It treats electrostatics and potential theory, steady currents and conduction, magnetostatics, induction and circuits, measurement instruments, magnetic materials, AC theory, Maxwell’s equations and electromagnetic waves, filters, transmission lines and waveguides, vacuum-tube electronics up to microwave devices, and noise; then the microscopic theory of dielectrics, electrons in metals and semiconductors, paramagnetism, ferromagnetism and antiferromagnetism, and magnetic resonance, ending with systems of units."
}